abstract: >-
  We benchmark machine learning approaches for voice-based
  Parkinson's
    disease telediagnosis using recordings from 252 participants (188 PD, 64 controls). Four dataset configurations (sex-agnostic, sex-aware, male-only, female-only) were   evaluated across six classifiers and two feature selection methods under subject-level   nested cross-validation with ADASYN oversampling. Best models achieved MCC up to 0.674, with SHAP analysis revealing sex-dependent vocal biomarkers: MFCC features drove female classification while TQWT and baseline features dominated male classification. Results highlight the importance of sex-specific modeling and class imbalance correction for reliable early PD screening.
